flowchart TB
accTitle: Four CoALA memory responsibilities and retrieval boundary
accDescr: Working memory stores active scoped context. Episodic memory stores reviewed experience. Semantic memory stores admitted facts. Procedural memory stores governed procedure versions. Cross-store retrieval produces typed results, followed later by B1 selection and B3 workspace admission.

    WM[Working memory<br/>active scoped context]
    EP[Episodic memory<br/>reviewed experience]
    SM[Semantic memory<br/>admitted facts]
    PM[Procedural memory<br/>governed versions]
    WM --> RET[Cross-store retrieval]
    EP --> RET
    SM --> RET
    PM --> RET
    RET --> RESULT[Typed retrieval result]
    RESULT -. later selection .-> B1[B1 memory selection<br/>Chapter 21]
    B1 -. later admission .-> B3[B3 workspace<br/>Chapter 21]
